"Runs Richards on fructus, which can't load the benchmark by its name like
 Harness and Run do. The argument is the number of inner iterations,
 default 1.

 THIS IS A CUT-DOWN RICHARDS: EACH ITERATION DOES A TENTH OF THE WORK OF THE
 ARE-WE-FAST-YET ONE, SO ITS RESULTS DON'T COMPARE WITH FULL RUNS. See
 Richards/Scheduler.som."
RunRichards = (
    run: args = (
        | innerIterations |
        innerIterations := args length > 1
            ifTrue: [ (args at: 2) asInteger ]
            ifFalse: [ 1 ].
        (Richards new innerBenchmarkLoop: innerIterations)
            ifTrue: [ 'Richards (CUT DOWN, NOT AWFY SIZE): ok' println ]
            ifFalse: [
                'Richards (CUT DOWN, NOT AWFY SIZE): incorrect result' println.
                system exit: 1 ]
    )
)
